<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">July 16, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 139 of the Iran–US War</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-07-16T07:00 UTC</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v48.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      The Iran–US conflict entered its most intense phase since the June 17 MOU collapse, with CENTCOM strike packages reaching within 30km of Tehran and Iran's ballistic missile command striking US bases in Jordan — with only a 20% probability of an official Iranian halt in the next 72 hours (<span class="cite">F1</span>) — while the Strait of Hormuz sat frozen at approximately 10% of pre-war transit volume, with the market recovery path constrained by suspended coalition demining and only a 25% probability of any recovery to 30/day by September 15 (<span class="cite">F4</span>).
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">6 active · last reasoned 2026-07-16</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM (≤72h)</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F1 · 2026-07-16-iran-halts-counter-strikes-by-july-19</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran announce an official halt or suspension of counter-strikes against US military assets before EOD 2026-07-19?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">20%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 20% (2026-07-16)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-19</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Iran Foreign Ministry spokesperson Baghaei stated on July 16 that Iran has 'no plans for negotiations under military coercion'; IRGC struck a US military base in Jordan with ballistic missiles on July 15 in response to US strikes near a Tehran children's hospital. Under the current US strike tempo — CENTCOM expanding to targets around Tehran and Iran's missile province — Iran is extremely unlikely to announce a formal halt within 72h. The 20% accounts for the possibility that Trump's threatened infrastructure strikes (power plants, bridges) could trigger an Iranian tactical pause to buy negotiating space via Qatar/Pakistan channels.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if an official Iranian MFA statement or IRGC command spokesperson publicly announces a halt, suspension, or cessation of counter-strikes against US military assets, carried by IRNA or two independent TIER1 sources, before EOD 2026-07-19.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IRNA or two independent TIER1 sources (Reuters/AP/AFP/Al Jazeera/CNN). A named MFA or IRGC spokesperson statement required.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>A tactical lull in strikes without an official announcement does NOT count; 'maximum restraint' or 'defensive posture only' language without explicit halt announcement = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO; proxy strikes by Hezbollah or Houthis are not Iranian state strikes and do not trigger resolution.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC General or MFA spokesperson publicly announces strike suspension</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">No Iranian strikes on US or allied military assets for 24+ consecutive hours</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F2 · 2026-07-16-iran-us-formal-session-by-july-30</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a formally convened US-Iran negotiating session (direct or via named mediator) be held before EOD 2026-07-30?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">30%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 30% (2026-07-16)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-30</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Iran FM Baghaei confirmed on July 16 that Iran has 'no plans for negotiations'; Trump stated on July 15–16 that strikes would intensify unless Iran 'gets to the table,' explicitly threatening power plants and bridges. Qatar and Pakistan confirmed shuttle diplomacy continuing as of July 14. The 30% reflects the structural tension: Iran's stated refusal to negotiate vs. the escalating threat of infrastructure strikes that may create conditions for Iran to recalculate. The June-to-MOU precedent took 16 days from suspension to formal session; a comparable cycle could produce talks by July 30.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a TIER1 source reports a formally convened direct or indirect negotiating session — in person or by confirmed videoconference — between named US and Iranian principals or senior envoys, with a named mediator or host (Oman, Qatar, Pakistan, Saudi Arabia, or any UN-endorsed host), between 2026-07-16 and 2026-07-30.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two independent TIER1 sources (Reuters/AP/AFP/Al Jazeera/CNN/CNBC) OR one TIER1 + official US State Dept or Iran MFA statement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Written message exchanges, relay diplomacy, or mediator shuttle visits without a convened session = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO; Trump or US-side claims of talks 'continuing' without Iranian confirmation of a convened session = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran MFA or Araghchi confirms a session is scheduled or has been held</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar PM or Pakistan PM announces a convened session readout</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F3 · 2026-07-16-hormuz-demining-resumes-by-aug-15</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will coalition mine-clearing operations in the Strait of Hormuz actively resume before EOD 2026-08-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">30%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 30% (2026-07-16)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">UK-France coalition minehunting vessels deployed to the region by July 4–6 (RFA Lyme Bay as mother ship; France's two minehunters) and were in position to begin limited operations in Omani waters before the July 6–7 vessel strikes forced a suspension. The July 8 MOU collapse and resumed CENTCOM naval blockade created an operational environment in which MCM operations carry strike risk. Approximately 80 mines remain in the main navigation channel. Resumption within 30 days requires either a new ceasefire framework or a unilateral UK/France decision to operate under hostile conditions — both of which remain possible given European energy exposure.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a TIER1 source confirms mine-countermeasure operations (US, UK, French, or multinational coalition) have actively recommenced in the Strait of Hormuz or its Omani approaches, between 2026-07-16 and 2026-08-15.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters/AP/AFP/Bloomberg/Lloyd's List OR named UK/France/US naval command or Pentagon statement confirmed by TIER1.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Vessel positioning, movement into theater, or stated intent without confirmed active operations = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO; coalition MCM in Omani waters on the main navigation corridor counts; MCM in Persian Gulf proper (not Hormuz) does not.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">UK or French naval command confirms MCM sortie or mine neutralization in Hormuz corridor</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">New US-Iran ceasefire or framework explicitly authorizes coalition MCM operations</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F4 · 2026-07-16-hormuz-30-transits-7day-by-sept-15</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Strait of Hormuz reach &gt;=30 commercial transits/day (7-day avg) before EOD 2026-09-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">25%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 25% (2026-07-16)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Hormuz transits collapsed from single-day peaks of ~52 (June 24–25) to approximately 10/day by July 12–16 following the MOU collapse, resumed CENTCOM naval blockade, and July 6–8 vessel strikes. Approximately 80 mines remain in the main navigation corridor. P&amp;I war-risk insurance is running at ~8× pre-crisis levels with 6 major clubs having withdrawn cover. Reaching 30/day (7-day average) within 61 days requires resumed MCM operations and insurer re-engagement — neither established in current posture. 25% reflects the ~90-day time-constant for previous Hormuz recovery cycles under more favorable conditions.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IMF PortWatch or equivalent AIS tracker records &gt;=30 commercial transits/day averaged over any consecutive 7-day window between 2026-07-16 and 2026-09-15.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IMF PortWatch (primary) + one TIER1 shipping report (Reuters/Bloomberg/Lloyd's List); if PortWatch unavailable, two independent AIS aggregators required.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Naval-escorted convoys count toward the transit total; one-off surge days not part of a 7-day average do not qualify; data gap &gt;3 consecutive days in PortWatch = AMBIGUOUS-OPEN until data restored.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">PortWatch 7-day transit average rising above 15/day (trend confirmation)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Major P&amp;I club reinstates Hormuz transit cover or reduces war-risk surcharge below 3×</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5 · 2026-07-16-iran-us-new-framework-by-sept-30</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the US and Iran agree to a new written ceasefire framework (MOU or equivalent) before EOD 2026-09-30?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">40%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 40% (2026-07-16)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-30</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">The Islamabad MOU (June 17) collapsed by July 8 after approximately 21 days. Both parties retain structural incentives for a second framework: Iran faces economic devastation from the Hormuz closure and US strikes; the US faces energy price shocks and allied pressure. The prior MOU took approximately 16 days from Iran's June 1 suspension to the June 17 signing — a comparable cycle could produce a new framework within the 76-day window. Qatar and Pakistan confirmed shuttle diplomacy continuing July 14. 40% reflects meaningful probability given both sides' structural vulnerabilities, balanced against Iran's current 'no negotiations' posture and Trump's stated intention to escalate to infrastructure.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if the US and Iran publicly confirm a new written ceasefire agreement, MOU, or equivalent framework document reducing active hostilities, between 2026-07-16 and 2026-09-30, with acknowledgment from both governments confirmed by TIER1.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two independent TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/CNBC/Al Jazeera) OR one TIER1 + official statements from both US State Dept and Iran MFA.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Verbal announcements without a signed or digitally confirmed text = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO; a ceasefire that only one party announces = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO; a tactical pause in strikes lasting &lt;72h without a signed framework = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar or Pakistan PM announces a draft framework text has been agreed</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran MFA formally reverses 'no negotiations' stance in official statement</span>
        </div>
