      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (30%):</strong> Both sides accept an unofficial tactical lull without a formal framework — analogous to the 21-day MOU cycle — producing a frozen-conflict stalemate through September with Hormuz at 10–20% of baseline transit volume.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (15%):</strong> Qatar and Pakistan broker a second MOU framework within the F5 window (by Sept 30, p=40%), reinstating coalition MCM and allowing Hormuz transit recovery toward the F4 threshold (30/day) by late September.</p>
